[size=5][b]Description[/b][/size]
Starfield's mission log only shows quests you've already picked up. [b]Completionist[/b] knows the full list in advance and tracks your progress automatically: every quest and activity in the game, and what you're still missing in each star system, planet and city.

It covers [b]251 quests and 94 activities[/b] from the base game, [b]Shattered Space[/b], [b]Terran Armada[/b], the [b]Free Lanes[/b] update and the [b]Trackers Alliance[/b]. Content you don't own is skipped automatically.

Found a quest that is tracked wrongly or listed in the wrong place? Please report it on [url=https://github.com/rixbrnn/starfield-completionist/issues]GitHub[/url] or in the Bugs tab.

[size=5][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install the requirements below.
[*]Install Completionist with Vortex or Mod Organizer 2 and make sure [b]StarfieldCompletionist.esm[/b] is enabled.
[*]Launch the game through SFSE and load your save. Safe to install mid-playthrough: progress is read from your save.
[*]Press [b]F7[/b] to open the menu, or open it from [b]Pause menu > Mod Settings > Launcher[/b].
[*][b]Playing with a controller?[/b] The menu is fully controller-supported. Assign a controller binding to [b]Open Completionist[/b] in [b]Pause menu > Mod Settings > Keybindings[/b]. We recommend [b]X + A[/b] (pressed together). There is no controller binding by default, so set one up once.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Log:[/b] only the quests you have found (in progress by type, completed, failed), like the game's own Missions menu.
[*][b]Here:[/b] what's missing, in progress and done where you are standing right now.
[*][b]Locations:[/b] every system, planet and city with its progress and quest list, including who gives each quest.
[*][b]Quests:[/b] each faction and the main story as a chain, in story order.
[*][b]Side quests:[/b] every side quest, all together or by system, planet and place.
[*][b]Activities:[/b] one-off activities (Earth landmarks, Clinic jobs, space encounters) and the small errands the game counts toward its own Activities stat. The menu also shows the game's own activity count.
[*][b]Objectives:[/b] select a quest in progress to expand it into the objectives the game shows (optional ones marked), and show any of them on the starmap.
[*][b]Track[/b] a started quest, or [b]show its start on the starmap[/b] with a course plotted, straight from the menu.
[*][b]Branching choices handled:[/b] the Crimson Fleet or UC SysDef ending, Foreknowledge or the regular path, Among the Stars or the full story. The paths you didn't take count as resolved, so 100% is always reachable.
[*][b]New Game+ aware:[/b] the NG+ intro variants count as One Small Step; Among the Stars and Foreknowledge only count once you've entered Unity.
[*][b]Manual override:[/b] mark any quest done or not done if detection gets it wrong. Saved in your save.
[*][b]Spoiler mode:[/b] hide the names of quests you haven't discovered.
[*][b]Notifications[/b] when you complete a quest or activity, with that place's progress, e.g. "Completed: Superfan (Neon 7/35)".
[*][b]Controller support[/b] with on-screen button prompts.
[/list]

[b]Controls[/b] (keyboard / controller). Open: F7, or the controller binding you assign in Mod Settings > Keybindings (we recommend X + A).
[list]
[*]Switch view (Log, Here, Locations, Quests, Side quests, Activities): Q / E (LB / RB)
[*]Switch filter / category tab: Z / C (flick the right stick left / right)
[*]Move: arrow keys (D-pad / left stick) · Open / close a quest's objectives: Enter (A) · Track: Enter (A) on an objective
[*]Show on map: R (X) · Sort: T (Y)
[*]Spoilers: X (View) · Mark done / not done: M (right-stick click)
[*]Close: Esc (B)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/106]Starfield Script Extender (SFSE)[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/3256]Address Library for SFSE Plugins[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/18326]OSF Settings[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/17711]OSF UI[/url] (needs the Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime, included with Windows 11)
[/list]
Without OSF UI and OSF Settings, tracking and notifications still work; only the menu is unavailable.

[b]Good to know[/b]
[list]
[*]Like any mod with a plugin, it disables achievements unless you use an achievement enabler.
[*]The menu needs the Steam version (SFSE doesn't support the Game Pass / Microsoft Store version).
[*]Quest start places are worked out from where each quest giver stands; a few may be off.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Contributing[/b][/size]
Completionist is open source. Report bugs, suggest features or contribute on GitHub: [url=https://github.com/rixbrnn/starfield-completionist]github.com/rixbrnn/starfield-completionist[/url]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/rixbrnn/starfield-completionist/issues/new/choose]Report a quest that is tracked wrongly or listed in the wrong place[/url]
[*]Quest data (places, questline order, branching choices) lives in plain JSON files, so fixes don't need any coding.
[*]Support for other mods' quests can be added the same way.
[/list]

